// AIRDROP_DISCOVER_BPLIST / AIRDROP_ASK_BPLIST: NO LONGER THE RESPONSE.
//
// These two constants were the /Discover and /Ask replies. They are now
// the REGRESSION REFERENCE and nothing else: the replies are built at ad_begin() by
// ad_bplist.h, because the name a sender shows on its share sheet is the
// ReceiverComputerName field inside them, and bplist strings are length-prefixed -- a
// different name moves every offset in the table and three 64-bit fields in the trailer.
//
// They are kept rather than deleted because they are what a real Mac has actually been
// accepting for the life of this project, and tools/test-bplist.sh asserts BYTE-EXACT
// equality between them and what the writer produces for the same name. Two definitions of
// the same thing is normally how a project ends up editing the wrong one -- the difference
// here is that the divergence is checked on every test run rather than hoped about.
//
